{ GNET_Primary_Generic_MA_Example - RESEARCH STRATEGY EXAMPLE, TradeStation 10.

  - Requires installed generic contract-3 support; development V39 import acceptance passed.
  - TradeStation compilation and this actual export remain platform acceptance steps.
  - LogicImplemented=true: this example implements the completed-bar MA crossover below.
  - Long entry: fast SMA crosses from at/below slow SMA to above it; next-bar market.
  - Optional short entry: the opposite crossover; ShortEnabled=false by default.
  - Exits: ProfitTicks target, StopTicks stop, or HoldBars time exit; single full position.
  - SMA state carries across sessions; no daily reset. Costs are declared per round trip.
  - Edit Inputs, GnetDeclaredInputs(), LogicFamily/LogicRevision and the marked entry block together.
  - This is a runnable MA example using the generic contract; the unfinished template stays separate.
  - Fixed Inputs are linked to the export; this scaffold does NOT export arbitrary per-bar diagnostics.
  - Supports single full-exit, next-bar-market positions only; no pyramid/partial/reversal support.
  - Current training adapter still requires one ES contract and reviewed fills/costs.
  - Broker validates observed positions; it does not independently reproduce custom entry rules.
  - Custody producer authorization and TradeStation Verify remain separate acceptance gates.

  - REQUIRED: Set ExportEnabled=true in the strategy attached to the chart.
  - REQUIRED: Set ExportInbox to the installed GNET incoming folder.
  - On this machine, ExportInbox="C:\GNET_Import\incoming".
  - BOTH inputs MUST be correct before this strategy can generate trades or export files.
  - Check the CHART'S strategy Inputs after every source replacement and Verify.
  - TradeStation can retain old chart Inputs even when the source defaults change.
  - ExportEnabled=false disables both primary trade generation and export in this strategy.

  - Create/Verify this technique as a STRATEGY, then apply it to a research chart.
  - It runs its own historical MA crossover and exports matching bars and positions together.
  - Keep your existing MA lengths, exit rules, quantity and cost settings.
  - Set chart strategy MaxBarsBack manually to 1; MA history is maintained internally.
  - Keep strategy automation OFF and intrabar order generation OFF; no real-time orders.
  - Use AutoSessions=true; the common inbox gets a fresh child for each export session.
  - Protected custody and the reviewed producer must be enabled before writing market rows.

  - Set AutoMetadata=true for automatic metadata resolution.
  - Set VolumeMode="unknown", PriceBasis="unknown" and ChartTimeZone="unknown".
  - Metadata-provider lookup timeout: 30 seconds; this is NOT the chart's bar timeframe.
  - The provider checks the last exported completed bar; it does not verify the entire tape.

  - The first 20 completed historical rows are buffered; the filename freezes after validation.
  - Historical rows are emitted one bar late to preserve same-second order.
  - The first real-time calculation closes the historical snapshot; live rows are excluded.
  - Offline, expired or closed-session charts can remain partial until calculation resumes.
  - Never promote a partial export using LastBarOnChartEx or a manually created ready marker.
  - Entry/exit timestamps are platform-reported values, not tick-tape execution proof.
  - EasyLanguage Verify, export closure, broker validation, approval and training are separate steps.
}

[IntrabarOrderGeneration = FALSE]

